WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.710
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.570
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.050
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.050
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.410
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.920
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.570
What's going on?

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.320
What's wrong?

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.660
Where's Sonic? Bring Sonic out!

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.120
We know you're here!

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:46.790
Oh no!

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.960
I'll pound 'em all away!

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.380
You can't! They'll think you're the enemy too!

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.300
But we can't leave things as is!

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:00.430
If we talk, we can clear things up! I'll talk to them!

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:01.890
Grandpa!

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:07.310
Sunlight vanished from our world.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:11.110
The Egg Moon blocked the path between the sun and the Earth.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:13.480
Everyone, please stop!

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:16.740
Eggman insists that it's a mechanical malfunction.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:22.410
Then he built Mirror Towers to provide sunlight to the people.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:28.250
Everyone thinks Eggman has changed and are thankful for his service.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.630
However, Sonic starts destroying the Mirror Towers.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.090
Why is this happening?

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.590
Why is this happening?

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:47.200
Episode 41

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:47.200
The Light is Ours!

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.570
I'm scared!

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.860
Bring Sonic out here!

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.320
Sonic isn't here!

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.410
You're hiding him!

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:07.330
Sonic has something in mind!

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.080
That's right!

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.960
Sonic is on our side!

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:16.380
Well, he was until now. But this time...

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:21.510
What's wrong with me? I'm not trusting Sonic!

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:22.800
Shut up!

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.810
They're Sonic's friends. Let's beat them up!

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.810
All of you!

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:31.850
Oh no!

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:37.780
This way!

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.840
This is the police! Break it up!

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:05.390
If you lay one finger on them, it means you're our enemy too.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.350
Understand?

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.400
Phew, I was worried about how things would turn out.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.660
I'm also fast when it comes to chasing people away.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.570
Are you okay, Chris?

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:28.080
Yeah.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:32.040
I'm sorry, Sonic.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.420
But...

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.170
Here I go!

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.430
How did you like that!

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:53.560
Mr. President, please stop Sonic!

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.860
You're asking us to do something? You can't handle it on your own?

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:01.530
What are you talking about? We've changed.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:07.160
We got rid of all our weapons so that we could become good citizens!

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.530
I see...

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.450
All right!

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.750
Assemble all GUN forces and stop Sonic!

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:15.750
Right!

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:36.890
The humans are going to defeat Sonic.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:39.610
This is an unexpected turn of events.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.440
Totally.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:45.650
Eggman is the greatest!

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:47.860
Eggman is our hero!

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.950
Everyone, thank you for your support!

00:05:54.950 --> 00:06:01.790
Sonic the hero has turned into a villain, and we've changed from villains into heroes.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.800
You never know how life turns out.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:17.940
What's wrong? Are you sleep-deprived because of your late nights?

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:21.650
No. There are strange radio waves coming from somewhere.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:25.990
Follow her!

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.760
It's dark.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:54.470
Poor thing...

00:06:58.520 --> 00:06:59.520
Knuckles!

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.900
Knuckles, can you do us a favor?

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:03.860
What is it?

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.440
Knuckles, you're the only one we can count on.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:09.490
It's all Sonic's fault that...

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.320
That we're...

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.270
You're in my way!

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:00.750
You're the only one who can stop Sonic!

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:04.460
Please stop Sonic!

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:05.880
Please!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:10.420
Please stop him, Knuckles!

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.720
Okay, I'll try.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.640
Thank you!

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:15.720
Knuckles!

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.050
Thank goodness!

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:18.890
Thank you.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:27.980
Sonic, I won't show you any mercy!

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:36.530
Chris?

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.120
What's the matter, Chris?

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:43.910
What?

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:46.080
You've been acting strange for awhile.

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.090
Really?

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.300
Yeah...

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:56.010
I can't understand why Sonic is doing this.

00:08:56.010 --> 00:09:01.640
I don't even know if I should trust him anymore.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.940
Sonic has something in mind!

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:06.810
That's right!

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:12.070
What can I do to trust Sonic, just like you two?

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:15.650
That's a hard question to answer.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.030
Because I like him.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:19.990
Because you like him?

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:29.000
But just when you think you caught him, he slips through your fingers and runs off.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.380
But that's okay because I like Sonic.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:41.100
Even if he runs to the edge of the world, I'll chase after him. And one day...

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.520
She trusts him because she likes him...

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.890
I see! That's all that matters!

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:48.270
There's no need to overthink this!

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.810
Thank you, Amy!

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.070
Yeah, I'll try my best!

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.940
Tails, let's go find Sonic!

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.530
I'll do it next week!

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:06.250
Sonic, how I feel about you is...

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:20.430
You've come.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.940
Hey, Knuckles. What's up?

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:37.820
Sonic!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.490
Hey!

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.910
You say hello with your fists?

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.660
Well, I guess that is something you would do.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.460
Fine, I'll take you on!

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:04.890
You're doing well, Knuckles!

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:06.680
You're much better than before!

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:09.560
I've learned a lot since coming here!

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:38.880
It's no good. This isn't a dome. It's a sphere.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:42.550
What's with this radio wave?

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:52.190
This is bad!

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:54.190
We have to stop them!

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:55.810
Leave it to me.

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:05.530
You still want to fight?

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:09.080
I won't stop until I beat you to a pulp!

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.500
Both of you, stop!

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.050
Sonic, Knuckles, please stop!

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.260
Don't interfere!

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:21.760
Sonic!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:25.890
I don't mind stopping, but he's so persistent.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.930
You're the one who's persistent!

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:32.600
Do you have any idea how many people are suffering because of you?

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.350
Because of me?

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:36.610
How dare you!

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.940
Sonic the Hedgehog!

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.160
Oh no!

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.870
You're completely surrounded!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.540
Stop resisting and surrender!

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:01.090
Don't do it!

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:02.970
I'll defeat Sonic!

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:04.420
Not you too, Knuckles!

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:08.640
Hey hey. Don't lose your temper. Let's all calm down.

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.390
Why you!

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.390
Stop it!

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:18.360
Why? Do you also think that Sonic is doing the right thing?

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:20.900
I don't know.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:23.610
But I trust Sonic!

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:26.700
Because I like Sonic!

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:30.240
Liking or hating him isn't the issue!

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:31.870
Give me a logical reason!

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.960
That thing is an eyesore.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:45.470
It doesn't allow me to enjoy my afternoon naps.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:47.880
That's a ridiculous reason!

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:50.550
I said that you shouldn't lose your temper.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:52.680
We just have to deal with it.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:56.270
We can't move it because it's malfunctioning.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:14:00.150
You can't move it? But it's moving.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:01.440
What?

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.530
The Earth revolves.

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:09.110
We wouldn't be experiencing this if the moon didn't also move accordingly.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.950
That's right!

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:15.330
That means the moon's orbital period changed.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:21.670
No, that's not enough to explain the cause because the Earth also revolves around the sun.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:27.630
It's too complicated!

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:32.430
That's right. It means that the Egg Moon is making complex movements.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:37.890
Eggman has an I.Q. of 300. If we were able to figure it out, that means he would've too.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.600
However, he didn't say anything.

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:44.820
That means Eggman is also responsible for this incident!

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:48.650
This feels great.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.540
It's not bad to be popular.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:59.410
Not bad at all. Right, Dr. Eggman?

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:03.880
Totally. It was worth all the effort.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:10.260
Dr. Eggman, what do you mean by effort?

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.890
What? You really don't know?

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:17.470
Do you really think this all happened by coincidence?

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.350
It didn't?

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:23.610
Of course not! Take a good look at them.

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:36.120
Eggman! Eggman!

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:38.040
What's going on?

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:48.210
When the Sunshine Ball emitted sunlight, I included a subliminal message telling them to adore me.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:52.880
So you planned this from the very beginning, Dr. Eggman?

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:54.550
I didn't know that!

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:56.390
That's not all.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:16:00.600
I've controlled the Egg Moon since the beginning!

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:06.400
The Eggman Empire will soon be realized!

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:10.860
So that's the situation.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:13.700
We're villains after all.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:18.660
That's the story.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:22.330
Why didn't you say so in the first place?

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:24.750
No one asked me.

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:26.630
I thought everyone knew.

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.210
How were we supposed to know?

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:33.550
That's the story.

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:37.890
This is Topaz. I must speak to the President immediately.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:46.060
What is it, Mr. President?

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:48.610
I trusted him...

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:50.400
Dr. Eggman!

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.610
So everything has come to light.

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:57.660
You've trampled our hearts!

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:02.620
You're the one who was tricked by the false information and distrusted Sonic.

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:05.080
That's because...

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:11.000
All those people support me, so would you like me to replace you as President?

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:12.840
Then what does that make me?

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:15.260
A hostage.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:19.100
What should we do?

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:23.390
Since we can't destroy the transmitter that controls the Egg Moon...

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:28.020
It means we have to destroy the receiver on the Egg Moon.

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:30.940
I'm counting on you, Knuckles.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:32.940
I'm going to be the pilot again?

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:35.320
I don't think that's a good idea.

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:37.910
I'll be the pilot.

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:43.620
We're counting on you.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:52.920
It's no good! The crowd is so thick that we can't make it through!

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:01.850
I've successfully sneaked in.

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:04.140
I will now begin the mission.

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:12.860
I'm done.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:16.570
How's this? It's a 1 egg bill.

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.240
I think it's good.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.910
And 1 Bocoe bill equals 100 egg bills.

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:23.370
1 Decoe bill equals 1000 egg bills.

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:27.500
Why are your bills worth more than mine?

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:41.050
Hey, Eggman!

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.510
We're putting an end to your shenanigans!

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:46.980
Oh yeah?

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.940
Go ahead and try!

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:50.690
All right!

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:52.690
Are you serious?

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:54.900
Don't you care what happens to the President?

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:57.110
I'm over here.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:19:00.160
What the... Since when?

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.450
Mission accomplished.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.370
See!

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:24.260
You're an excellent pilot, Mr. Tanaka.

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:28.600
It's been my dream since childhood to become an astronaut.

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:32.850
Over there, Knuckles!

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:35.940
So that's it!

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.300
Look, Helen.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:06.890
The blessing of the sun.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:29.580
Next time, let's watch the sunrise from the cruise ship.

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.790
What a lovely idea!

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:35.130
I did it!

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:39.340
What's wrong? You look depressed.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:43.130
It would've been better if it remained nighttime all the time.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:49.310
This is how things always end up.

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:51.680
It's the fate of being a villain.

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:55.810
However, villains never die! We'll try again!

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:05.530
Question number one:

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:10.490
The sum of the inner angles of a triangle is 360 degrees. Yes or No?

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.540
No!

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:18.130
Question number two:

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:24.590
The turboprop engine can generate more horsepower than a plane with a reciprocating engine.

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:26.760
Yes!

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:28.890
Question number three:

